Heliod puts a +1/+1 counter on a creature every time you gain life, and for {1}{W} gives another creature lifelink. Give Walking Ballista lifelink and every ping gains a life, which puts the counter right back on Ballista: unlimited damage from two cards, one of which is your commander. The rest of the deck finds Ballista or Triskelion and stops the table from doing anything about it.

# The commander
Heliod, Sun-Crowned :: three mana, indestructible. Whenever you gain life, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature or enchantment you control. {1}{W}: another target creature gains lifelink until end of turn.
Heliod is only a creature with five devotion to white, and the combo does not need him to be one. He just needs to be on the battlefield.
He is indestructible, so exile, bounce and tuck effects are what stop him. Hold Mother of Runes, Giver of Runes or a counterspell-style stax piece for those.

# Infinite combos — why this is Bracket 3.5
Heliod, Sun-Crowned + Walking Ballista :: cast Ballista with X of at least 1, pay {1}{W} to give it lifelink, then remove a counter to ping. You gain 1, Heliod puts a counter back on Ballista, repeat. Unlimited damage and life. Seven mana across two turns: Heliod (3) one turn, then Ballista with X = 1 (2) and the activation (2).
Heliod, Sun-Crowned + Triskelion :: the same loop with Triskelion, which enters with three counters already.
Walking Ballista + Agatha's Soul Cauldron :: if Ballista is in your graveyard, exile it with the Cauldron. Every creature you control with a +1/+1 counter gains its abilities, so give one of them lifelink with Heliod and loop the same way.
Two cards, with the commander as one of them, is exactly what Bracket 3 forbids and this Bracket 3.5 deck keeps.

# Tutor lines — what to fetch, and when
Every tutor in the deck can find Ballista. Pick the one that leaves mana for the activation the same turn.
Ranger-Captain of Eos -> Walking Ballista :: Ballista has mana value 0 in your library, so it counts as a one-drop. Three mana for the Captain, and you can sacrifice it to stop opponents casting noncreature spells on the combo turn.
Recruiter of the Guard -> Walking Ballista :: any creature with toughness 2 or less: Ballista (0) or Triskelion (1).
Ranger of Eos -> Walking Ballista :: two creatures of mana value 1 or less: Ballista plus Mother of Runes or Esper Sentinel.
Enlightened Tutor -> Walking Ballista :: it's an artifact, so Enlightened Tutor puts it on top. Cast it at an opponent's end step and draw it next turn.
Scrapyard Recombiner -> Triskelion :: sacrifice an artifact to tutor any Construct: Ballista, Triskelion, or the Recombiner itself.
Inventors' Fair -> Walking Ballista :: with three artifacts out, a land that tutors any artifact.
Buried Ruin -> Walking Ballista :: returns an artifact from your graveyard to hand.

# The stax shell — use it, but know it cuts both ways
These slow the table down while you assemble two cards. Most are symmetric, so play them when they hurt the opponents more than you.
Rule of Law :: one spell per turn for everyone. Your combo is one spell (Ballista) and an activation, so it still works.
Eidolon of Rhetoric :: the same, on a creature.
Archon of Emeria :: the same, and their nonbasic lands enter tapped.
Phyrexian Censor :: one non-Phyrexian spell each per turn, and non-Phyrexian creatures enter tapped.
Deafening Silence :: one noncreature spell per turn each.
Ethersworn Canonist :: artifact spells are exempt, so Ballista still resolves after another spell.
Thalia, Guardian of Thraben :: noncreature spells cost {1} more. Your combo pieces are creatures.
Chalice of the Void :: counters every spell with a chosen mana value. Pick a number your opponents use more than you do; set to 1, it also counters your Swords and Path.
Vexing Bauble :: counters spells cast with no mana. It also counters your own free Flawless Maneuver and an evoked Solitude.
Boromir, Warden of the Tower :: counters opponents' free spells, and sacrifices to protect your board.
Grand Abolisher :: nobody responds on your turn. The best card to have out on the combo turn.
Voice of Victory :: opponents can't cast spells on your turn.
Silence :: the one-turn version.
Orim's Chant :: target player can't cast spells this turn; kicked, nobody attacks.
Linvala, Keeper of Silence :: their creatures' activated abilities can't be used.
Karn, the Great Creator :: their artifacts' activated abilities can't be used.
Blind Obedience :: their artifacts and creatures enter tapped, and extort drains on every spell.
Authority of the Consuls :: their creatures enter tapped, and you gain a life each time. Each of those life gains is a Heliod counter.
Dauntless Dismantler :: their artifacts enter tapped; sacrifice it to destroy every artifact of a chosen mana value.
Aven Mindcensor :: their searches only see the top four cards.
Rest in Peace :: no graveyards. It also turns off your Agatha's Soul Cauldron line.
Grafdigger's Cage :: no creatures from graveyards or libraries, and no casting from either.
Weathered Runestone :: no permanents from graveyards or libraries.
Soulless Jailer :: no permanents from graveyards, and no noncreature spells from graveyard or exile.
Containment Priest :: creatures that weren't cast are exiled instead.
Calamity's Wake :: exile every graveyard and stop noncreature spells for the rest of the turn. Your Ballista is a creature spell, so cast it after.

# Answers and protection
Swords to Plowshares :: one mana, exile a creature.
Path to Exile :: the same.
Winds of Abandon :: a sorcery Path; overloaded, it hits every opposing creature.
Solitude :: flash, exile a creature; evoke it free by exiling a white card.
March of Otherworldly Light :: exile an artifact, creature or enchantment.
Generous Gift :: destroy any permanent.
Witch Enchanter :: destroy an artifact or enchantment, or play it as a land.
Aven Interrupter :: flash: exile a spell (it's plotted), and their graveyard and exile spells cost {2} more.
Reprieve :: return a spell to its owner's hand and draw.
Mother of Runes :: protection for a creature, at instant speed.
Giver of Runes :: the same, including from colourless.
Flawless Maneuver :: free while Heliod is out: your creatures are indestructible for the turn.
Angel's Grace :: split second: you can't lose this turn.
Talon Gates of Madara :: phase a creature out in response to removal.
Eiganjo, Seat of the Empire :: a land that deals 4 to an attacker.

# Cards and mana
The One Ring :: protection for a turn, then a card every upkeep.
Smothering Tithe :: Treasure whenever opponents draw.
Esper Sentinel :: taxes their first noncreature spell each turn.
Archivist of Oghma :: a card and a life whenever an opponent searches. The life is a Heliod counter.
Welcoming Vampire :: a card when a small creature enters, once a turn.
Mentor of the Meek :: pay {1} to draw when a small creature enters.
Trouble in Pairs :: draws when opponents attack you with two creatures, draw extra, or cast a second spell.
Serra Ascendant :: lifelink on turn one; a 6/6 flier at 30 life.
Emeria's Call :: two 4/4 Angels, or a land.
Land Tax :: three Plains a turn when behind on lands.
Archaeomancer's Map :: two Plains, then lands when opponents get ahead.
Weathered Wayfarer :: tutors any land when you're behind.
Deep Gnome Terramancer :: a Plains whenever an opponent puts a land onto the battlefield without playing it.
Sol Ring :: the usual.
Arcane Signet :: the usual.
Fellwar Stone :: the usual.
Mind Stone :: a rock that cashes in for a card.
Pearl Medallion :: white spells cost {1} less.
Lotus Petal :: free.
Mox Opal :: live with three artifacts.
Nykthos, Shrine to Nyx :: white mana equal to your devotion.
City of Traitors :: two mana until your next land drop.
Monumental Henge :: digs for a historic card: Ballista, Triskelion and every legend count.
Urza's Saga :: makes Construct tokens, then chapter III finds Sol Ring, Lotus Petal or Mox Opal.
Emergence Zone :: everything has flash for a turn.

# What to keep in an opening hand
Keep a land count of three, some acceleration, and either a combo piece or a tutor for it. Turn three Heliod, turn four or five Ballista with {1}{W} up.
Land one lock piece early (Rule of Law, Archon of Emeria, Grand Abolisher) to slow the table, but don't play two that also strangle you.
On the combo turn: Grand Abolisher or Silence first, then Ballista, then the activation.
